\meta{color-kernel-version}{0.5.0}
\meta{color-kernel-verified-date}{2026-07-14}
\meta{color-seed}{stable seed of public artifact alias}
\meta{color-selection}{first unused color matching the assigned trit}

\p{This public page lists every file in the locally verified offer surface as a snapshot-scoped anonymous artifact alias and assigns each file a deterministic color. It contains 88 files in 38 units: 77 requestable artifacts and 11 simulated tooling fixtures. The exact restricted inventory, filenames, paths, timestamps, hashes, accounts, host details, participant-like labels, and row linkages are intentionally not embedded.}
\p{A listing means that an artifact is locally present and that a governed request can be reviewed. It is not a license, consent record, blanket offer, or release authorization. Colors identify artifact aliases only; they do not identify people, sessions, devices, or physiological states.}
\p{Aliases are scoped to the snapshot date and are not cross-snapshot identities. Cite the snapshot date with every request.}
\subtree{
\title{Request Data}
\p{Use the private contact route published on the parent page with subject \code{[data request]}. Cite one or more public group, unit, or file aliases and the snapshot date from this page. Do not put private source values in a public issue or pull request.}
\p{State the smallest useful artifact set, intended use, requester and collaborators, onward-sharing plan, security controls, retention and deletion plan, and the applicable consent, ethics, privacy, rights, and release-authority basis. Review may return aggregate metadata, a schema, a redacted or derived subset, or nothing.}
}
\subtree{
\title{Color and GF(3) Method}
\p{Artifact aliases are ordered deterministically by source class, anonymous unit, and artifact kind. Complete triples receive \code{-1}, \code{0}, \code{+1}; any trailing aliases receive \code{0}. Each alias is assigned a stable seed; the generator selects the first unused color whose canonical trit matches the assigned trit. The ledger has 29 minus, 30 zero, and 29 plus assignments, so the trit sum is zero and therefore conserved modulo three. Files remain separate colored artifacts under their anonymous cohort and unit.}
}
\subtree{
\title{Complete Available-File Ledger}
\p{The ledger below contains all 88 locally present files, totaling 21,036,101,577 bytes. Real-data artifacts remain request-only. Simulated entries are listed for completeness and are tooling fixtures, not physiological data.}
