\subtree{
\title{Maintenance and Verification}
\p{The checked-in generator verifies the canonical raw manifest against local bytes, rejects missing or unknown companion types, separates real and simulated runs from their recorded flags, requires the expected unit and file counts, assigns all colors in one clean color process, checks uniqueness and GF(3) conservation, emits only allowlisted public fields, and separately writes a mode-0600 private alias-to-source registry with integrity hashes. A maintainer must regenerate and review this page whenever the private offer surface or color-kernel revision changes.}
}
